  "description": "First entry with a communication area present and a full page below: the NOT CDEMO-PGM-REENTER arm at :115-119 over the ten records app/jcl/DUSRSECJ.jcl loads. :116 sets CDEMO-PGM-REENTER, :117 MOVE LOW-VALUES TO COUSR0AO discards every screen field the payload carried, :118 performs PROCESS-ENTER-KEY - whose selection scan at :151-185 therefore always reaches WHEN OTHER - and :227 restarts the count at zero before PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD. The forward loop at :300-306 reads ten records and steps WS-IDX to 11 through the COMPUTE at :304 (gate G28), which is what page size TEN means here: exactly ten rows are filled and the eleventh iteration never runs (gate G39). :308 is then true, so :309-310 computes page 1, and the look-ahead READNEXT at :311 reaches the end of the file - setting USER-SEC-EOF, painting 'You have reached the bottom of the page...' and sending the map from inside :640 - after which :315 sets NEXT-PAGE-NO. WS-MESSAGE is not cleared between sends, so that message survives into the final image. COUSR00C sends the map three times here (:640, :329 and :119); UserMenuController records all three on its work area, but its published handler exposes only the transmission the terminal is left displaying, and widening that API would break the single-public-method property UserMenuControllerTest pins - so the earlier two are asserted there, in the user package, and all 59 fields of the final one are asserted here.",
